Step 1c: Intention Extraction

You are given a list of outcomes from a dialogue.

=== OUTCOMES ===
[
  {
    "outcome id": "outcome 1",
    "outcome": "German language learning session on vocabulary review, directions, and grammar"
  },
  {
    "outcome id": "outcome 2",
    "outcome": "Session time frame and activity plan decision"
  },
  {
    "outcome id": "outcome 3",
    "outcome": "Vocabulary review drill (Translation Tennis)"
  },
  {
    "outcome id": "outcome 4",
    "outcome": "Directions vocabulary drills and exercises"
  },
  {
    "outcome id": "outcome 5",
    "outcome": "Integration of user-provided tips into the exercise bank"
  },
  {
    "outcome id": "outcome 6",
    "outcome": "Grammar instruction and roleplay practice (Imperative, Prepositions, and Separable Verbs)"
  },
  {
    "outcome id": "outcome 7",
    "outcome": "Grammar instruction and roleplay exercise on prepositions and formal imperative"
  }
]

(1) Identify distinct **intentions** (high-level goals or purposes) that these
outcomes serve. (2) Assign each outcome to exactly one intention.

Output JSON only:
{ "intentions": [ {"intention id": "I1", "intention": "short label"},
{"intention id": "I2", "intention": "another label"} ], "outcome to intention":
[{"outcome id": "outcome 1", "intention id": "I1"}, ...] }
- Every outcome id appears exactly once in outcome to intention. Use intention id
from the intentions list.
